## Blends round a flat face's tangent loops, built directly (no booleans):
## the edges where a flat face (the cap) meets walls ruled away from it.
## Planes, cylinders and cones about the cap's normal, and surfaces swept
## straight along one way (B-spline sweeps, an earlier fillet's strips, a
## cylinder along a slanted upright), as an extrusion's sides (straight or
## tapered) or an earlier fillet's strips are. The top of a box whose
## uprights were filleted is such a loop: lines and the fillets' sections,
## tangent where they meet; so is a tapered one's.
##
## The blend is a 2D section (a circle's arc, a G2/G3 B-spline, or a
## chamfer's line) carried along the edge in the frame of the way into the
## cap and the wall's ruling (cap_rows.lucb). As OpenCASCADE and Parasolid
## do for a rolling ball along a curve, the strip over a curved edge or a
## slanted wall is approximated: each row of its section's control points
## is fitted along the edge, so its rows on the cap and the wall are those
## faces' new boundaries. Lines and arcs with walls that keep one corner
## stay exact: a line's rows are lines, an arc's arcs; square ones are a
## cylinder or plane along a line, a torus or cone about an arc.
##
## The cap's loop moves onto the contacts on it, each wall's edge onto its
## contact (the wall's ruling at the corner moved along), and each joint's
## seam (the line between two walls, along their common ruling) is
## shortened; joints get one section edge both strips share. Every vertex
## of a picked edge is such a joint, or an open end: the loop goes on
## tangentially into an edge that is not picked. There the blend runs out
## as Fusion 360's does (cap_runout.lucb): carried on past the end and
## trimmed by the faces it runs into; where the face going on does not turn
## away from it, the strip stops in the section's plane, a flat end face
## fills the corner between the section and the sharp edge going on, and
## the seam is split at the wall's contact. Anything else is declined
## (blend.lucb's booleans).

## A picked edge of a cap loop: its cap and wall faces, the side of its
## cap normal its cap lies on (`sign`: the way into the cap is `sign`
## (n x the edge's carrier tangent)), the cap's normal toward the wall
## (`into_wall`), whether the edge is convex, how its wall runs away from
## it (`ruling`: cap_rows.lucb; `s0`, `s1` a plane's at its ends, `sweep`
## a sweep's way), and what it becomes: its contact edges on the cap
## (`outer`) and the wall (`inner`), and its strip's surface and sense.
struct CapSide:
    var edge: usize
    var cap: usize
    var wall: usize
    var sign: f64
    var into_wall: Vector3
    var convex: bool
    var ruling: i64
    var s0: Vector3
    var s1: Vector3
    var sweep: Vector3
    var outer: i64
    var inner: i64
    var surface: i64
    var sense: bool

## The builder: the body `w`, the result `out` (begun as a copy of the
## body, so its points, edges and surfaces keep their numbers), the blend
## (`reach`: a fillet's radius, a chamfer's size; `weight`: a G1 section's
## middle weight, the chain's corner's; a chamfer's `chamfer` sides, and
## whether the cap takes their first distance: `cap_first`), and for each body edge its picked
## side (-1), whether it is a seam, and its new seam (-1, a split seam's
## upper part in `uppers`), for
## each body vertex its contacts on the cap and wall, its section (-1),
## whether it is an open end (the edge going on there: `continues`), its
## run-out (`runout_of`, into `runouts`; -1: a flat end) and a flat end's
## line from its cap contact to it.
struct Cap:
    var w: const Shape*
    var out: Shape
    var reach: f64
    var law: const RadiusLaw*?
    var round: bool
    var continuity: i64
    var weight: f64
    var chamfer: const ChamferSides*?
    var cap_first: bool
    ## Fusion's Tangency weight of a G2 or G3 section (fillet_section).
    var tangency: f64
    ## A G1 variable fillet at weight 1 round a closed loop: the ball rolled
    ## (cap_rolled.lucb), its sections degree 5.
    var rolled: bool
    var balls: SampledBalls
    var sides: Growing[CapSide]
    var side_of: Growing[i64]
    var is_seam: Growing[bool]
    var seams: Growing[i64]
    var uppers: Growing[i64]
    var on_cap: Growing[i64]
    var on_wall: Growing[i64]
    var sections: Growing[i64]
    var open: Growing[bool]
    var continues: Growing[i64]
    var end_lines: Growing[i64]
    var runouts: Growing[Runout]
    var runout_of: Growing[i64]
    var name: Growing[u8]

    func close():
        self.out.close()
        self.sides.close()
        self.side_of.close()
        self.is_seam.close()
        self.seams.close()
        self.uppers.close()
        self.on_cap.close()
        self.on_wall.close()
        self.sections.close()
        self.open.close()
        self.continues.close()
        self.end_lines.close()
        self.runouts.close()
        self.runout_of.close()
        self.name.close()
        self.balls.close()

    func at(id: i64) -> Vector3:
        return self.out.points.items[(usize)id]

    ## A straight out edge from point `a` to `b`.
    func line(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64!:
        let pa = self.at(a)
        let span = self.at(b).subtract(pa)
        let length = span.length()
        if length <= self.w.tolerance: error(invalid, "a blend would make an edge of no length")
        let c = try self.out.add_carrier(Carrier(0, pa, span.multiply_scalar(1.0 / length), Vector3(), 0.0, 0.0, -1))
        return try self.out.add_edge(ShapeEdge(c, 0.0, length, a, b))

    ## A B-spline out edge over its whole domain, from point `a` to `b`:
    ## from its first control point to its last (`forward`), or back.
    func spline(a: i64, b: i64, net: const Vector3[], weights: const f64[], knots: const f64[], degree: i64, forward: bool) -> i64!:
        let index = try self.out.store_spline(net, weights, knots, degree, Matrix4())
        let c = try self.out.add_carrier(Carrier(2, Vector3(), Vector3(), Vector3(), 0.0, 0.0, index))
        let low = knots[(usize)degree]
        let high = knots[net.length]
        return try self.out.add_edge(ShapeEdge(c, low if forward else high, high if forward else low, a, b))

## Edges `chosen` of `w` blended round their caps (see the file's header):
## filleted to `size` (`continuity` 1 to 3) when `round`, its radius
## changing along the chain by `law` when given (`size` then its largest),
## else chamfered (by `sides` when given: chamfers.lucb); none when they are
## not all such loops (the booleans then try).
pub func cap_blend(w: const Shape*, chosen: const usize[], size: f64, round: bool, continuity: i64, tag: str, sides: const ChamferSides*? = none, law: const RadiusLaw*? = none, tangency: f64 = 1.0) -> interop.Reference[CadModel]?!:
    var made = try new_cap(w, size, round, continuity)
    defer made.close()
    let b = &made
    b.tangency = tangency
    b.law = law
    if not try cap_eligible(b, chosen): return none
    try chamfer_first(b, sides)
    try chain_weight(b)
    b.rolled = rolled_cap(b)
    if b.rolled: try cap_balls(b)
    try cap_room(b)
    try cap_contacts(b)
    for k in 0..<b.sides.count: try cap_strip(b, k)
    try cap_sections(b)
    return try cap_result(b, tag)

func new_cap(w: const Shape*, size: f64, round: bool, continuity: i64) -> Cap!:
    var out = empty_shape(w.tolerance)
    errdefer out.close()
    for p in w.points.view(): try out.points.push(p)
    for c in w.carriers.view(): try out.carriers.push(c)
    for edge in w.edges.view(): try out.edges.push(edge)
    for sp in w.splines.view(): try out.splines.push(sp)
    for p in w.spline_points.view(): try out.spline_points.push(p)
    for x in w.spline_weights.view(): try out.spline_weights.push(x)
    for k in w.spline_knots.view(): try out.spline_knots.push(k)
    for s in w.surfaces.view():
        try out.surfaces.push(try Surface(s.kind, s.origin, s.x, s.z, s.radius, s.angle, s.points, s.weights, s.ku, s.kv, s.nu, s.nv, s.du, s.dv))
    var made = Cap(w, out, size, none, round, continuity, math.sqrt(0.5), none, true, 1.0, false, SampledBalls(Growing[Vector3](), Growing[f64](), 1.0), Growing[CapSide](), Growing[i64](), Growing[bool](), Growing[i64](), Growing[i64](), Growing[i64](), Growing[i64](),
                   Growing[i64](), Growing[bool](), Growing[i64](), Growing[i64](), Growing[Runout](), Growing[i64](), Growing[u8]())
    errdefer made.close()
    try made.side_of.fill(w.edges.count, -1)
    try made.is_seam.fill(w.edges.count, false)
    try made.seams.fill(w.edges.count, -1)
    try made.uppers.fill(w.edges.count, -1)
    try made.on_cap.fill(w.points.count, -1)
    try made.on_wall.fill(w.points.count, -1)
    try made.sections.fill(w.points.count, -1)
    try made.open.fill(w.points.count, false)
    try made.continues.fill(w.points.count, -1)
    try made.end_lines.fill(w.points.count, -1)
    try made.runout_of.fill(w.points.count, -1)
    return made

## A chamfer's `sides` on the builder, and which face of the loops takes
## their first distance: the same for every side (a section is shared at
## each joint), or an error.
func chamfer_first(b: Cap*, sides: const ChamferSides*?) -> !:
    b.chamfer = sides
    if b.round or sides == none: return
    for k in 0..<b.sides.count:
        let side = b.sides.items[k]
        let on_cap = first_face(sides, side.edge, side.cap)
        if k == 0: b.cap_first = on_cap
        elif on_cap != b.cap_first: error(invalid, "this chamfer's first distance would change faces along its loop: flip it, or chamfer the loop's edges apart")

## Whether the loop's fillet rolls a ball (Fusion's G1 at weight 1 along a
## law that changes): a closed loop (no open end).
func rolled_cap(b: const Cap*) -> bool:
    let law = b.law else return false
    if not b.round or b.continuity != 1 or b.tangency != 1.0: return false
    var changes = false
    for r in law.radii.view():
        if r != law.radii.items[0]: changes = true
    if not changes: return false
    for open in b.open.view():
        if open: return false
    return true

## The G1 section's middle weight, sin(θ/2) for the chain's corner of
## cosine λ (√½ square): the corner at the first side's start (a slanted
## sweep's corner changes along it; its sections are then near-circles).
func chain_weight(b: Cap*) -> !:
    let side = b.sides.items[0]
    let (lambda, _) = try corner_at(b, &side, b.w.edges.items[side.edge].t0)
    b.weight = math.sqrt((1.0 - lambda) * 0.5)

## The way into side `side`'s cap at its carrier's parameter `t`, and how
## it turns (its derivative by `t`).
func into_cap(b: const Cap*, side: const CapSide*, t: f64) -> (Vector3, Vector3)!:
    let w = b.w
    let n = w.surfaces.items[(usize)w.faces.items[side.cap].surface].z
    let (_, d1, d2) = try w.derivatives(w.edges.items[side.edge].carrier, t)
    let crosswise = n.cross(d1)
    let turning = n.cross(d2)
    let length = crosswise.length()
    if length <= 1e-300: error(invalid, "a blend's edge stops along it")
    let u = crosswise.multiply_scalar(side.sign / length)
    let du = turning.multiply_scalar(1.0 / length).subtract(crosswise.multiply_scalar(crosswise.dot(turning) / (length * length * length)))
    return (u, du.multiply_scalar(side.sign))

## Each vertex's contacts on the cap (its contact distance into the cap)
## and the wall (that far along the ruling), the open ends' run-outs, each
## seam shortened to its wall contact (a joint's, a run-out's), or split
## there (a flat end's: its upper part meets the end face).
func cap_contacts(b: Cap*) -> !:
    let w = b.w
    for side in b.sides.view():
        let edge = w.edges.items[side.edge]
        for end in 0..<(usize)2:
            let v = edge.start if end == 0 else edge.end
            if b.on_cap.items[(usize)v] >= 0: continue
            let t = edge.t0 if end == 0 else edge.t1
            let (u, _) = try into_cap(b, &side, t)
            let (lambda, c) = try corner_at(b, &side, t)
            let s = try ruling_at(b, &side, t)
            let p = w.points.items[(usize)v]
            b.on_cap.items[(usize)v] = try b.out.add_point(p.add(u.multiply_scalar(c)))
            b.on_wall.items[(usize)v] = try b.out.add_point(p.add(s.multiply_scalar(try wall_distance(b, lambda, try reach_at(b, &side, t)))))
    try cap_runouts(b)
    for v in 0..<w.points.count:
        if flat_end(b, v): b.end_lines.items[v] = try b.line(b.on_cap.items[v], (i64)v)
    for g in 0..<w.edges.count:
        let seam = w.edges.items[g]
        if not b.is_seam.items[g]: continue
        let low = b.on_wall.items[(usize)seam.start]
        let high = b.on_wall.items[(usize)seam.end]
        if low < 0 and high < 0: continue
        let a = low if low >= 0 else seam.start
        let z = high if high >= 0 else seam.end
        b.seams.items[g] = try b.line(a, z)
        # At an open end the part above the contact stays, the way the seam
        # runs.
        if low >= 0 and flat_end(b, (usize)seam.start): b.uppers.items[g] = try b.line(seam.start, low)
        if high >= 0 and flat_end(b, (usize)seam.end): b.uppers.items[g] = try b.line(high, seam.end)

## Whether vertex `v` is an open end that stops flat (no run-out).
func flat_end(b: const Cap*, v: usize) -> bool:
    return b.open.items[v] and b.runout_of.items[v] < 0

## The largest blend the loops take, an error when the blend is not
## smaller: each contact on the cap must stay short of where the edge's
## offset folds (its radius of curvature toward the cap), and each seam
## between walls must keep some length (its whole length, or half when
## blends shorten it at both ends).
func cap_room(b: const Cap*) -> !:
    let w = b.w
    var most = 1.0e300
    var what = "this curved edge"
    # The contacts are the radius times the corner's factor (1 when square).
    var factor = 1.0
    for side in b.sides.view():
        let edge = w.edges.items[side.edge]
        for k in 0..<(usize)5:
            let t = edge.t0 + (edge.t1 - edge.t0) * (f64)k / 4.0
            let (lambda, c) = try corner_at(b, &side, t)
            let r = try reach_at(b, &side, t)
            factor = math.max(factor, math.max(c, try wall_distance(b, lambda, r)) / r)
        most = math.min(most, try offset_room(b, &side))
    var ends = Growing[i64]()
    defer ends.close()
    try ends.fill(w.points.count, 0)
    for side in b.sides.view():
        let edge = w.edges.items[side.edge]
        ends.items[(usize)edge.start] = 1
        ends.items[(usize)edge.end] = 1
    for g in 0..<w.edges.count:
        if not b.is_seam.items[g]: continue
        let seam = w.edges.items[g]
        let shortened = ends.items[(usize)seam.start] + ends.items[(usize)seam.end]
        if shortened == 0: continue
        let height = w.points.items[(usize)seam.end].subtract(w.points.items[(usize)seam.start]).length() / (f64)shortened
        if height < most:
            most = height
            what = "the height of its walls"
    if b.reach * factor >= most: try too_large(b.round, b.reach, most / factor, what)

## An error: a blend of `size` is too large for `what`; it must be less
## than `most`.
func too_large(round: bool, size: f64, most: f64, what: str) -> !:
    var buffer: u8[256]
    let text = try strings.format(buffer, f"a fillet radius of {rounded_text(size)} is too large for {what}: it must be less than {rounded_text(most)}") if round else try strings.format(buffer, f"a chamfer of {rounded_text(size)} is too large for {what}: it must be less than {rounded_text(most)}")
    let owned = try interop.copy_text(text)
    if let owner = owned.owner: _ = ownership.pool_object(owner)
    error(invalid, owned.value)

## How far side `side`'s cap contact may go in before its offset of the
## edge folds back (where the edge curves toward the cap: its radius of
## curvature there); very large when it never does.
func offset_room(b: const Cap*, side: const CapSide*) -> f64!:
    let edge = b.w.edges.items[side.edge]
    var least = 1.0e300
    for k in 0..<(usize)65:
        let t = edge.t0 + (edge.t1 - edge.t0) * (f64)k / 64.0
        let (_, d1, _) = try b.w.derivatives(edge.carrier, t)
        let (_, du) = try into_cap(b, side, t)
        let turning = du.dot(d1)
        if turning < 0.0: least = math.min(least, d1.dot(d1) / -turning)
    return least

## Whether side `side` keeps one corner all along with its wall's ruling
## square to the edge (no skew): a line between planes whose seams are
## parallel and square to it, an arc on a cylinder or cone about the cap's
## normal. Its strip is then a cylinder, plane, torus or cone.
func regular_side(b: const Cap*, side: const CapSide*) -> bool!:
    if b.law != none: return false
    let w = b.w
    let edge = w.edges.items[side.edge]
    let kind = w.carriers.items[(usize)edge.carrier].kind
    if kind == curve_circle: return side.ruling == ruling_cone
    if kind != curve_line or side.ruling != ruling_between: return false
    let along = w.carriers.items[(usize)edge.carrier].x
    return side.s0.subtract(side.s1).length() <= 1e-12 * side.s0.length() and math.abs(side.s0.dot(along)) <= 1e-12 * side.s0.length()

## Side `k`'s contact edges and strip surface.
func cap_strip(b: Cap*, k: usize) -> !:
    let side = b.sides.items[k]
    let w = b.w
    let edge = w.edges.items[side.edge]
    let carrier = w.carriers.items[(usize)edge.carrier]
    let cap_start = b.on_cap.items[(usize)edge.start]
    let cap_end = b.on_cap.items[(usize)edge.end]
    let wall_start = b.on_wall.items[(usize)edge.start]
    let wall_end = b.on_wall.items[(usize)edge.end]
    let corner = w.points.items[(usize)edge.start]
    let (u0, _) = try into_cap(b, &side, edge.t0)
    var empty_points: Vector3[]
    var empty_numbers: f64[]
    # A corner of cosine λ: the cap's contact c from it, the wall's its leg
    # along the ruling (μ of it along the normal); a fillet's center r off
    # the cap.
    let (lambda, c) = try corner_at(b, &side, edge.t0)
    let mu = math.sqrt(1.0 - lambda * lambda)
    let regular = try regular_side(b, &side)
    if carrier.kind == curve_line and regular:
        b.sides.items[k].outer = try b.line(cap_start, cap_end)
        b.sides.items[k].inner = try b.line(wall_start, wall_end)
        let along = carrier.x.multiply_scalar(1.0 if edge.t1 > edge.t0 else -1.0)
        if b.round and b.continuity == 1:
            let axis = corner.add(u0.multiply_scalar(c)).add(side.into_wall.multiply_scalar(b.reach))
            try b.out.surfaces.push(try Surface(1, axis, try b.at(cap_start).subtract(axis).normalized(), along, b.reach, 0.0, empty_points, empty_numbers, empty_numbers, empty_numbers, 0, 0, 0, 0))
            return try finish_strip(b, k)
        if not b.round:
            let normal = try along.cross(b.at(wall_start).subtract(b.at(cap_start))).normalized()
            try b.out.surfaces.push(try Surface(0, b.at(cap_start), along, normal, 0.0, 0.0, empty_points, empty_numbers, empty_numbers, empty_numbers, 0, 0, 0, 0))
            return try finish_strip(b, k)
    elif carrier.kind == curve_circle and regular:
        # Concentric arcs: the cap's contact a circle of the radius moved c,
        # the wall's moved c λ and lowered c μ.
        let radial = w.points.items[(usize)edge.start].subtract(carrier.origin)
        let outward = 1.0 if u0.dot(radial) > 0.0 else -1.0
        let radius = carrier.a + c * outward
        let c_cap = try b.out.add_carrier(Carrier(1, carrier.origin, carrier.x, carrier.y, radius, radius, -1))
        b.sides.items[k].outer = try b.out.add_edge(ShapeEdge(c_cap, edge.t0, edge.t1, cap_start, cap_end))
        let down = try wall_distance(b, lambda, b.reach)
        let wall_radius = carrier.a + down * lambda * outward
        let lowered = carrier.origin.add(side.into_wall.multiply_scalar(down * mu))
        let c_wall = try b.out.add_carrier(Carrier(1, lowered, carrier.x, carrier.y, wall_radius, wall_radius, -1))
        b.sides.items[k].inner = try b.out.add_edge(ShapeEdge(c_wall, edge.t0, edge.t1, wall_start, wall_end))
        if b.round and b.continuity == 1:
            # A torus about the arc's axis, its tube's center the ball's path.
            let center = carrier.origin.add(side.into_wall.multiply_scalar(b.reach))
            try b.out.surfaces.push(try Surface(5, center, carrier.x, carrier.x.cross(carrier.y), radius, b.reach, empty_points, empty_numbers, empty_numbers, empty_numbers, 0, 0, 0, 0))
            return try finish_strip(b, k)
        if not b.round:
            # A cone through both contact circles, opening its own way.
            let opening = wall_radius - radius
            let axis = side.into_wall if opening > 0.0 else side.into_wall.multiply_scalar(-1.0)
            let origin = carrier.origin if opening > 0.0 else lowered
            let start_radius = radius if opening > 0.0 else wall_radius
            try b.out.surfaces.push(try Surface(2, origin, carrier.x, axis, start_radius, math.atan2(math.abs(opening), down * mu), empty_points, empty_numbers, empty_numbers, empty_numbers, 0, 0, 0, 0))
            return try finish_strip(b, k)
    # The section swept along the edge: rows of control points, each exact
    # (a line's, an arc's) or fitted, sharing their knots.
    var a = Growing[f64]()
    defer a.close()
    var z = Growing[f64]()
    defer z.close()
    var ku = Growing[f64]()
    defer ku.close()
    var wu = Growing[f64]()
    defer wu.close()
    let du = try section_at(b, lambda, b.reach, &a, &z, &ku, &wu)
    var net = Growing[Vector3]()
    defer net.close()
    var kv = Growing[f64]()
    defer kv.close()
    var wv = Growing[f64]()
    defer wv.close()
    let dv = try along_rows(b, &side, a.count, &net, &kv, &wv)
    let nv = wv.count
    let nu = a.count
    if b.sides.items[k].outer < 0:
        if carrier.kind == curve_line and side.ruling == ruling_between and b.law == none:
            # Exact lines between the contacts.
            b.sides.items[k].outer = try b.line(cap_start, cap_end)
            b.sides.items[k].inner = try b.line(wall_start, wall_end)
        else:
            # The first and last rows: an arc's run from its start over
            # [0, 1], a fitted one on the carrier's parameter.
            let forward = edge.t1 > edge.t0 or (carrier.kind == curve_circle and side.ruling == ruling_cone)
            b.sides.items[k].outer = try b.spline(cap_start, cap_end, net.view()[..<nv], wv.view(), kv.view(), dv, forward)
            b.sides.items[k].inner = try b.spline(wall_start, wall_end, net.view()[(nu - 1) * nv..<nu * nv], wv.view(), kv.view(), dv, forward)
    var weights = Growing[f64]()
    defer weights.close()
    for i in 0..<nu:
        for j in 0..<nv: try weights.push(wu.items[i] * wv.items[j])
    try b.out.surfaces.push(try Surface(3, Vector3(), Vector3(), Vector3(), 0.0, 0.0, net.view(), weights.view(), ku.view(), kv.view(), (i64)nu, (i64)nv, du, dv))
    try finish_strip(b, k)

## Side `k`'s strip is the surface just made: its sense, outward (away
## from the material) at the section's middle halfway along.
func finish_strip(b: Cap*, k: usize) -> !:
    let side = b.sides.items[k]
    let edge = b.w.edges.items[side.edge]
    let surface = (i64)b.out.surfaces.count - 1
    b.sides.items[k].surface = surface
    let t = (edge.t0 + edge.t1) * 0.5
    let (u, _) = try into_cap(b, &side, t)
    let s = try ruling_at(b, &side, t)
    let tangent = try (try b.w.tangent(edge.carrier, t)).normalized()
    let spread = try s.subtract(tangent.multiply_scalar(s.dot(tangent))).normalized()
    let bisector = try u.add(spread).normalized()
    let outward = bisector.multiply_scalar(-1.0 if side.convex else 1.0)
    let corner = try b.w.at(edge.carrier, t)
    # A point of the strip there: the circle's middle (G1), the chamfer's,
    # or near the B-spline's (its normal by parameters, so near is enough).
    let surf = &b.out.surfaces.items[(usize)surface]
    var normal = Vector3()
    if surf.kind == surface_spline:
        let u_mid = (surf.ku[(usize)surf.du] + surf.ku[(usize)surf.nu]) * 0.5
        let v_low = surf.kv[(usize)surf.dv]
        let v_high = surf.kv[(usize)surf.nv]
        # Halfway along the rows is halfway along the edge (a B-spline's
        # rows run on its parameter, a line's and an arc's over [0, 1]).
        normal = try surface_normal_checked(surf.points, surf.weights, surf.nu, surf.nv, surf.du, surf.dv, surf.ku, surf.kv, u_mid, (v_low + v_high) * 0.5)
    else:
        # The arc's middle, on the bisector from its center to the corner;
        # the chamfer's, between its contacts.
        let (lambda, c) = try corner_at(b, &side, t)
        let center = corner.add(u.multiply_scalar(c)).add(side.into_wall.multiply_scalar(b.reach))
        let middle = center.add((try corner.subtract(center).normalized()).multiply_scalar(b.reach)) if b.round else corner.add(u.multiply_scalar(c * 0.5)).add(s.multiply_scalar(try wall_distance(b, lambda, b.reach) * 0.5))
        normal = try normal_at(surf, middle, b.w.tolerance * 100.0)
    b.sides.items[k].sense = normal.dot(outward) > 0.0
    # A fitted strip is parametrized with its normal into the material (its
    # rows reversed when not): the tessellator's fallback for an unevenly
    # sampled B-spline face (an open end's strip beside a notched cap) fails
    # to converge for the other orientation.
    if surf.kind == surface_spline and b.sides.items[k].sense: try reverse_rows(b, surface)

## Surface `at` of the result (a strip, its rows along its edge) with its
## rows running the other way: the same surface, its normal turned.
func reverse_rows(b: Cap*, at: i64) -> !:
    let old = &b.out.surfaces.items[(usize)at]
    let nu = (usize)old.nu
    let nv = (usize)old.nv
    var net = Growing[Vector3]()
    defer net.close()
    var weights = Growing[f64]()
    defer weights.close()
    for i in 0..<nu:
        for j in 0..<nv:
            try net.push(old.points[i * nv + nv - 1 - j])
            try weights.push(old.weights[i * nv + nv - 1 - j])
    var knots = Growing[f64]()
    defer knots.close()
    let low = old.kv[0]
    let high = old.kv[old.kv.length - 1]
    for q in 0..<old.kv.length: try knots.push(low + high - old.kv[old.kv.length - 1 - q])
    let turned = try Surface(surface_spline, Vector3(), Vector3(), Vector3(), 0.0, 0.0, net.view(), weights.view(), old.ku, knots.view(), old.nu, old.nv, old.du, old.dv)
    var replaced = b.out.surfaces.items[(usize)at]
    replaced.close()
    b.out.surfaces.items[(usize)at] = turned
    let index = (usize)b.sides.count
    for k in 0..<index:
        if b.sides.items[k].surface == at: b.sides.items[k].sense = false

## Each vertex's section, from its cap contact to its wall contact, shared
## by the strips meeting there (or ending: an open end's): a chamfer's
## line, a circle's arc (G1: an exact circle at a square corner, else the
## rational arc), or the G2/G3 B-spline.
func cap_sections(b: Cap*) -> !:
    let w = b.w
    var a = Growing[f64]()
    defer a.close()
    var z = Growing[f64]()
    defer z.close()
    var ku = Growing[f64]()
    defer ku.close()
    var wu = Growing[f64]()
    defer wu.close()
    var net = Growing[Vector3]()
    defer net.close()
    for side in b.sides.view():
        let edge = w.edges.items[side.edge]
        for end in 0..<(usize)2:
            let v = (usize)(edge.start if end == 0 else edge.end)
            if b.sections.items[v] >= 0: continue
            let t = edge.t0 if end == 0 else edge.t1
            let (u, _) = try into_cap(b, &side, t)
            let s = try ruling_at(b, &side, t)
            let (lambda, _) = try corner_at(b, &side, t)
            let corner = w.points.items[v]
            let head = b.on_cap.items[v]
            let tail = b.on_wall.items[v]
            if not b.round:
                b.sections.items[v] = try b.line(head, tail)
                continue
            let tangent = try (try w.tangent(edge.carrier, t)).normalized()
            let r = try reach_at(b, &side, t)
            if b.rolled:
                # The rolled section there (cap_rolled.lucb), degree 5.
                try cap_rolled_section(b, &side, t, &net)
                let degree = try section_at(b, 0.0, r, &a, &z, &ku, &wu)
                b.sections.items[v] = try b.spline(head, tail, net.view(), wu.view(), ku.view(), degree, true)
                continue
            if b.continuity == 1 and b.tangency == 1.0 and math.abs(s.dot(tangent)) <= 1e-12 * s.length():
                # A circle's arc square to the edge, from the cap's contact
                # round to the wall's: π - θ (under a Tangency weight the
                # conic's spline, below).
                let (_, c) = try corner_at(b, &side, t)
                let center = corner.add(u.multiply_scalar(c)).add(side.into_wall.multiply_scalar(r))
                let x = try b.at(head).subtract(center).normalized()
                let to_tail = b.at(tail).subtract(center)
                let y = try to_tail.subtract(x.multiply_scalar(to_tail.dot(x))).normalized()
                let carrier = try b.out.add_carrier(Carrier(1, center, x, y, r, r, -1))
                b.sections.items[v] = try b.out.add_edge(ShapeEdge(carrier, 0.0, math.pi - math.acos(lambda), head, tail))
                continue
            let degree = try section_at(b, lambda, r, &a, &z, &ku, &wu)
            net.clear()
            for i in 0..<a.count: try net.push(corner.add(u.multiply_scalar(a.items[i])).add(s.multiply_scalar(z.items[i])))
            b.sections.items[v] = try b.spline(head, tail, net.view(), wu.view(), ku.view(), degree, true)
